WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.666
Divergent plates move apart. New oceanic crust forms at the ridge,

00:00:04.666 --> 00:00:08.982
so this is a constructive boundary. Identify it from relative motion.

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:14.609
Convergent plates move together. At a subduction zone, old oceanic lithosphere

00:00:14.609 --> 00:00:18.867
sinks and is recycled. That is the destructive boundary in the

00:00:18.867 --> 00:00:19.255
review.

00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:25.147
Transform plates slide past: a conservative boundary. Crust is neither created

00:00:25.147 --> 00:00:29.944
nor consumed. On a map, count connected plate regions, then identify

00:00:29.944 --> 00:00:31.252
each boundary's motion.
